{%- comment -%}
  Product node — Product + Offer, rendered from sections/main-product.liquid and
  sections/featured-product.liquid.

  Task: WORK/Clients/Monteiro-Fabrics/tasks/schema-product-additional-property.md

  WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
  The buyer questions that matter here are SPEC questions — "coated upholstery fabric, Crib 5,
  400.000 Martindale, bleach-cleanable". Those numbers used to exist on the page only as prose, so
  the Product node said the product exists and nothing about what distinguishes it. The
  `additionalProperty` array below is that missing half.

  SOURCES — every value is read straight off `product.metafields.custom.*`. Nothing is computed,
  defaulted or inferred, so a product with thin metafields simply emits fewer properties. The two
  constants that are NOT metafields:
    - "Martindale cycles" / "ISO 5470-2" on abrasion — the method is stated identically on every
      datasheet in `APP/mf-knowledge/products/collections/` and in the live product descriptions.
    - the `@id` references, which point at snippets/structured-data-organization.liquid.

  ⚠️ NEVER add a property whose value is not certified or on a datasheet. An empty metafield, or the
  literal "-" placeholder (ELECTRA uses it for colour fastness), emits no line at all — a missing
  property is honest, a guessed one is not.

  ⚠️ KNOWN DATA DEFECT, MUST BE FIXED BEFORE THIS SHIPS (2026-08-21):
  `custom.abrasion_resistance` was checked on all 26 active products against the catalogue linked
  from each product page (plus the print catalogues in
  WORK/Clients/Monteiro-Fabrics/reference/knowledge/product-catalogues/). Nineteen are right.
  These are not:
    - LIMA and MANTA            → metafield ≥400.000, catalogue ≥150.000
    - PURE CONVERTIBLE          → metafield ≥400.000, catalogue 150.000
    - PURE MOVE [3/3]           → metafield ≥200.000, catalogue 150.000 (the BLT bi-elastic group).
                                  200.000 appears in NO document.
    - LAGUNA                    → the two official catalogues disagree with each other:
                                  print MAI2025 (DC 062.01) says 400.000, the web catalogue linked
                                  from the live product page says ≥150.000. Same weight, thickness
                                  and composition in both. Unresolvable without the technical team.
    - PURE MOVE [2/3]           → the page mixes article groups: ARATA/NASCAR/PHILIP PES are
                                  400.000 but FRANK PES is 150.000. One figure per page cannot be
                                  right for this page.
    - CHANCE [1/7], [5/7], [6/7] → the AGO2026 catalogue footnotes "*metallic colours: lower
                                  abrasion resistance (150.000 cycles)"; these are the pages that
                                  carry metallic shades. The Essentials_Chance.pdf currently linked
                                  from the product pages has no such footnote.
  The fix belongs in the metafield, not here — it also feeds the visible spec block. Until it is
  corrected, this snippet publishes a wrong certified number, machine-readably, on those products.

  Offer carries no price — see WORK/Clients/Monteiro-Fabrics/decisions/2026-08-20-offer-sem-preco.md
  Every variant is priced 0.00 because the cart is a free-sample mechanism, not a shop; emitting
  that zero told every machine reader the fabrics are free. Price is quote-only.

  Offer carries no availability either — same decision note, dated amendment of 2026-08-31.
  This used to emit InStock/OutOfStock from `variant.available`. That flag is true whenever
  inventory is not tracked, and the whole store runs tracked:false — so the conditional had exactly
  one outcome and InStock was never an assertion anyone made about stock, only an artefact of not
  tracking it. The client fact of 2026-08-27 is that the assigned salesperson handles stock case by
  case; nobody verifies fabric stock here. And this Offer is for the FABRIC — the free sample is
  deliberately not modelled as a 0-euro Offer of it — so InStock was a machine-readable claim about
  fabric stock that nothing supported. Same reasoning that removed the price.

  What remains is what is true: url + seller. Expect Search Console to report two missing fields on
  Product (price and availability). That is the accepted cost, not a regression.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign mf_org_id = shop.url | append: '/#organization'

  assign mf_rs = '~~'
  assign mf_fs = '||'
  assign mf_props = ''

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.type.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Material' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs
  endif

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.engraving1.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Engraving' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs
  endif

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.abrasion_resistance.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Abrasion resistance' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_fs | append: 'Martindale cycles' | append: mf_fs | append: 'ISO 5470-2' | append: mf_rs
  endif

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.resitencia_ao_alchool.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Alcohol resistance' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs
  endif

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.colour_fastness_to_light.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Colour fastness to light' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs
  endif

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.antibacterial1.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Antibacterial' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs
  endif

  assign mf_v = product.metafields.custom.metalized_colour1.value | strip
  if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-'
    assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Metalized colours' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%} flammability2 is a list metafield — one PropertyValue per certification. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for mf_cert in product.metafields.custom.flammability2.value -%}
  {%- assign mf_v = mf_cert | strip -%}
  {%- if mf_v != blank and mf_v != '-' -%}
    {%- assign mf_props = mf_props | append: 'Fire certification' | append: mf_fs | append: mf_v | append: mf_rs -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  "name": {{ product.title | json }},
  "url": {{ shop.url | append: product.url | json }},
  {%- if product.featured_media.preview_image -%}
    {%- assign image_size = product.featured_media.preview_image.width | append: 'x' -%}
    "image": [
      {{ product.featured_media.preview_image.src | img_url: image_size | prepend: "https:" | json }}
    ],
  {%- endif -%}
  "description": {{ product.description | strip_html | json }},
  {%- if current_variant.sku != blank -%}
    "sku": {{ current_variant.sku | json }},
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    product.vendor holds a marketing tagline ("Knitted look. Timeless shades."), not a brand name,
    so it must not be used here. The brand is the company, declared once in the Organization node.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "brand": { "@id": {{ mf_org_id | json }} },
  {% if current_variant.barcode != blank %}
    "mpn": {{ current_variant.barcode | json }},
  {% endif %}
  {%- if mf_props != blank -%}
    {%- assign mf_records = mf_props | split: mf_rs -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The comma is written BEFORE each entry, counted off mf_emitted, rather than off forloop.last.
      A record that fails the size check is skipped, so forloop.last cannot be trusted to mark the
      last thing actually emitted — that is how you get a trailing comma and an unparseable node.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    "additionalProperty": [
      {%- assign mf_emitted = 0 -%}
      {%- for mf_record in mf_records -%}
        {%- assign mf_field = mf_record | split: mf_fs -%}
        {%- if mf_field.size >= 2 -%}
          {%- if mf_emitted > 0 %},{% endif %}
          {
            "@type": "PropertyValue",
            "name": {{ mf_field[0] | json }},
            "value": {{ mf_field[1] | json }}
            {%- if mf_field.size >= 3 -%}, "unitText": {{ mf_field[2] | json }}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if mf_field.size >= 4 -%}, "measurementTechnique": {{ mf_field[3] | json }}{%- endif -%}
          }
          {%- assign mf_emitted = mf_emitted | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ],
  {%- endif -%}
  "offers": [
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
      {
        "@type" : "Offer",
        {%- if variant.sku != blank -%}
          "sku": {{ variant.sku | json }},
        {%- endif -%}
        "url" : {{ shop.url | append: variant.url | json }},
        "seller": { "@id": {{ mf_org_id | json }} }
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
</script>
